WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:00.400
We talked

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.369
about the 60 Minutes interview

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:02.736
last night

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:04.471
that Lesley Stahl did with Congressman

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.806
Marjorie Taylor Greene.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.174
I think we have a clip.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:08.942
Let's play it for people

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.810
who didn't see the whole thing.

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:13.013
Are you saying

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:14.180
that you don't stand by

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.782
what's on your social media?

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:15.949
Well,

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:16.950
of course I stand for

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.451
what's on my social media,

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.753
but at times not

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:21.588
You're not always in control.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:23.423
We have all kinds of people

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:25.358
that work on our social media.

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.794
Did you apologize for your position

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.529
on Parkland, Florida?

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:30.663
What was my position

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:31.531
on Parkland, Florida?

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.432
That it was a false

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:32.799
I don't know

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.134
if you actually have my post.

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:36.002
No, I never said Parkland was a false.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:36.336
Did you?

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:37.537
No, I've never said that.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.839
We fact-checked before.

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:41.241
I got to this interview.

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:41.908
Have you fact

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.009
checked all my statements

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:44.778
from kindergarten through 12th grade

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:45.845
and in college?

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:48.348
The Democrats are a party of pedophiles.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.717
I would definitely say so.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.886
They support grooming children.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:54.687
They are not pedophiles.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.156
Why would you say that?

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:58.758
Democrats, Democrats support

00:00:58.958 --> 00:00:59.793
even Joe Biden.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.061
The president himself

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.595
supports children

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:03.630
being sexualized

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.432
and having transgender surgeries.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.933
Sexualizing children is what

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.234
pedophiles do to children.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:10.670
Wow.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:12.772
Okay.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:15.608
She is someone who, in just her second

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:19.079
term in Congress, has got a lot of power,

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:20.847
a lot more power than she had before,

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:22.415
thanks to Kevin McCarthy.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:25.018
Fundraises a lot of money.

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:27.720
So, yes, there are critics who are saying

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.422
why did 60 minutes go for that platform?

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.224
I think Leslie Saul did a good job

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:31.991
in that interview.

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.093
And I just wonder what you took

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:34.360
away from it. Yes.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.361
I mean, there's a fellow Leslie

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:36.062
Stahl family.

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:36.830
I can't fault them.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.531
I mean, 60 minutes is interviewed,

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:41.334
you know, rapists and hitmen and all

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.669
sorts of people,

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:44.504
you know, who are who are in the news.

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:45.371
I mean, I think that

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:46.439
one of the most interesting things

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:46.906
happening here

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:47.440
is that Marjorie

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.209
Taylor Greene, who obviously, as you say,

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:50.510
is a significant figure.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:51.744
Whatever you think of her has

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:54.314
a lot of power in Washington, is

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.882
it was made a decision

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:57.851
to attempt to kind of

00:01:57.851 --> 00:01:59.519
get to a more mainstream place

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:01.054
by doing things like 60 minutes.

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:03.223
We have a big story like Diego Baez

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:04.090
coming out this morning

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.425
and said before about really about how

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:07.227
this is part of her media strategy

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:08.128
to embrace the media

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:09.462
she criticizes around the Sanders

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.397
for not talking to the media enough

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.233
and yet at the same time

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.635
she's trying to become more mainstream

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:16.302
she she's still

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:18.838
calling Democrats pedophiles and she and

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:19.906
I don't know

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:20.940
if you can do both of those things

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:21.608
at the same time

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:23.843
she is trying to sort of say look

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.578
this is the Republican Party now

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:26.579
sort of take us or leave us

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:27.280
and you have to deal with

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.314
us on our terms.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.282
But she

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:30.517
but she is also walking away

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:32.185
from some of the crazier substance,

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:32.652
some of it

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.220
and saying she was misled,

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.522
saying she was like a normal

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:37.157
American is basically true.

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:37.991
A normal American

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:38.925
who was reading all sorts

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:40.293
of nonsense on Facebook and believing

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:40.727
a lot of it.

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.095
I also found it really interesting

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:42.729
that she told

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:43.263
Leslie Stahl

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.731
that the reason she got in

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:45.698
and ran and left

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.167
the construction business, etc.,

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:47.967
is because of her

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.035
fellow Republicans,

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:51.271
not because of Democrats.

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:51.571
Yeah.

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:52.105
I mean, you know,

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:53.907
I think she really does embody

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:54.908
this kind of new Trump

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:55.775
movement in the party.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:57.410
Whether it totally takes over the party

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.112
or not is an open question.

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:00.380
But I think the idea,

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.681
which was a bit of always

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.582
a bit of a fantasy

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.551
that journalists, that Democrats

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:04.984
just sort of

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:05.852
can ignore,

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.587
that wing of the Republican Party

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:08.454
is totally over.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:09.756
And the 60 Minutes interview

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:11.591
sort of codifies that in a certain way.

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:12.158
It just

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:13.560
you're not putting her in that group

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:14.160
when you're

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:14.794
when you're talking about

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.629
who else 60 minutes is interview.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:17.397
I just know how people

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:19.165
say thanks

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.700
for letting me clean that up, Caitlin.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.301
No, I'm just saying

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:21.901
they've interviewed people

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.469
far more controversial

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.137
than Marjorie Taylor

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:26.005
against her prominence in the Republic.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.140
But that is a constant struggle

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:27.907
that we have been dealing

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:29.442
with since Trump

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.977
or Trumpism is

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:32.345
who do you give a platform to?

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:33.980
Who is legitimate and who's not in this

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.548
especially when you have election deniers

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.050
and people who are just,

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:37.317
you know,

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:39.252
making things up as they go along with.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.220
No, not based.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:40.887
In fact,

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:42.722
do you actually put them

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:44.457
on traditional media to elevate them?

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.858
That is a struggle that,

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:46.893
you know, that we all face.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.962
So I can understand why. Yeah.

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.463
And you have to be fast on your feet

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:51.197
as a journalist

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:53.132
the way the way Lesley Stahl is.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:53.600
Yeah.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.401
Just as interesting why she did it

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:56.936
as why they did it.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.104
To your point,

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:59.572
Ben Smith, thanks for bringing the table.

00:03:59.572 --> 00:03:59.939
Thank you.

